<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 305 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 305 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 305 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1,600 MLN  1,600 MLN  1,600 MLN 1,600 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    437 MLN    1,276 MLN 1,581 MLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    80 MLN*    283 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS				  517 MLN*</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED LATE ASSISTANCE	 =	    =	   305 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (=UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 357 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING OCTOBER 16, 17 and 18 AT</p>
<p>5-23/32 PCT, AND AT 1300 GMT 39 MLN BILLS/FRG FOR RESALE TO MKT IN EQUAL AMOUNTS ON OCT 16-18.</p>
</text>
